---
Title: Function blocks
---

A line that starts with a complete function runs it:

function() { return 'A plain string, inserted as it stands.' }

function() {
	return { block: 'Returned *markdown*, lexed as a block.' };
}

function(x) is how a paragraph of prose might begin; it stays prose.

Mid-paragraph, a line such as
function(x) continues the paragraph rather than cutting it.

function() { return null }

function() { throw new Error('boom') }

After the error, the build carries on.
